      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIa-b-5",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Describe the process of transcription.</li><li>Identify the role of RNA polymerase.</li><li>Explain mRNA processing.</li><li>Diagram the flow from DNA to mRNA.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Transcription</strong> — DNA → mRNA.</li><li><strong>RNA polymerase</strong> — enzyme that makes mRNA.</li><li><strong>Template strand</strong> — the DNA strand read by RNA polymerase.</li><li><strong>Codon</strong> — 3 nucleotides coding for an amino acid.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Steps of Transcription</h4><ol><li><strong>Initiation:</strong> RNA polymerase binds to the promoter</li><li><strong>Elongation:</strong> RNA polymerase reads the template strand and adds RNA nucleotides</li><li><strong>Termination:</strong> RNA polymerase reaches the terminator; mRNA is released</li></ol><h4>B. mRNA Processing (Eukaryotes)</h4><ul><li>5' cap added</li><li>Poly-A tail added</li><li>Introns removed (splicing)</li><li>Exons joined</li></ul><h4>C. DNA → mRNA Example</h4><p>DNA: TAC GGA TTC → mRNA: AUG CCU AAG</p>",
      "activity1": {
