      "title": "Mutations & Their Effects",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIIa-b-5",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Define genetic mutation.</li><li>Differentiate gene mutations from chromosomal mutations.</li><li>Describe effects of mutations.</li><li>Relate mutations to genetic disorders.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Mutation</strong> — change in DNA sequence.</li><li><strong>Point mutation</strong> — single nucleotide change.</li><li><strong>Frameshift</strong> — insertion/deletion shifts reading frame.</li><li><strong>Chromosomal mutation</strong> — changes in chromosome structure or number.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Types of Point Mutations</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Silent</td><td>No change in amino acid</td></tr><tr><td>Missense</td><td>Different amino acid</td></tr><tr><td>Nonsense</td><td>Premature stop codon</td></tr></tbody></table><h4>B. Frameshift Mutations</h4><ul><li>Insertion or deletion of nucleotides</li><li>Shifts the reading frame</li><li>Usually more severe</li></ul><h4>C. Chromosomal Mutations</h4><ul><li>Deletion, duplication, inversion, translocation</li><li>Aneuploidy (e.g., Down syndrome)</li></ul>",
